<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Jan-May oil product exports up 64 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Jan-May oil product exports up 64 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's oil product exports surged 64 percent to 93.5 million barrels in the first five months of 1997 against 56.9 million barrels a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Friday.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement a rise in oil products output triggered the increase in exports.</p>
<p>On the other hand, the nation's imports fell 25.4 percent to 85.6 million barrels in January to May from 114.8 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>The ministry did not give a breakdown by each product.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
